Unit commitment, reserves, ramping and chronological state (@pe-commitment: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/MOST-User-Manual-1-3-1.lingua#r_3BNCVR190YKFZ0YMSWHV1PMJ99", #source "../sources/Redefining-Resource-Adequacy-ESIG.lingua#r_0HBM3TV8RE50TSK5D34E4TTC4G", #source "../sources/Convex-Optimization-Boyd-Vandenberghe.lingua#r_54EB992HDGH8YV8BEV5PT5CYHA", #electrical-power-engineering "../planning/Adequacy-energy-limits-and-correlated-failures.lingua#r_1A4E6T6AW67E09WQ2C1NPRH3Y7") { r_0QFNTTAR35VZZ8WSRF0ZNBGKBC
**Read:** [MOST User’s Manual, version 1.3.1](../sources/MOST-User-Manual-1-3-1.lingua#r_3BNCVR190YKFZ0YMSWHV1PMJ99), entire manual, complete formulations and substantial examples; [Redefining Resource Adequacy for Modern Power Systems — ESIG](../sources/Redefining-Resource-Adequacy-ESIG.lingua#r_0HBM3TV8RE50TSK5D34E4TTC4G), whole chronological/dependence and reliability treatment; [Convex Optimization — Boyd and Vandenberghe](../sources/Convex-Optimization-Boyd-Vandenberghe.lingua#r_54EB992HDGH8YV8BEV5PT5CYHA), complete applicable optimization foundations and limits.

A multiperiod schedule links decisions through machine state, startup/shutdown, ramp, minimum operation, fuel/resource and storage/service constraints. Commitment is not the same as continuous economic dispatch. A resource that is cheap when running may take time, energy and supporting services to become available.

Derive a small original two/three-period problem with explicit initial and terminal conditions. Compare unconstrained dispatch, ramp-limited operation and a commitment choice. Include reserve as a deliverable response under actual headroom/rate/energy conditions rather than a free extra MW label. State scenario probabilities and nonanticipativity if uncertain futures share decisions.

Read all of [MOST User’s Manual, version 1.3.1](../sources/MOST-User-Manual-1-3-1.lingua#r_3BNCVR190YKFZ0YMSWHV1PMJ99), reconstruct its complete formulation and compare one authorized example with an independent small solution. Investigate storage terminal-value assumptions, correlated resource/load conditions and a changed event sequence. A cost-minimizing schedule is conditional on the represented uncertainty and physical model; it does not by itself demonstrate adequacy or real-time stability. Preserve each model limitation and the evidence needed to support an operational decision.

**Continue:** [Adequacy, energy limits and correlated failures](../planning/Adequacy-energy-limits-and-correlated-failures.lingua#r_1A4E6T6AW67E09WQ2C1NPRH3Y7).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
